  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Productive Social Safety Net Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the scale up of the Productive Social Safety Net which will reach  1 million households, and these households are the poorest 15%.  through the provision of conditional Cash Transfers, Green Public Works and Livelihood Enhancement.  This programme will aim to improve the opportunities available to the poorest communities by reducing the depth of income poverty, improving food consumption and increasing their resilience to climate-related shocks.  DFID will also support central government to develop and strengthen systems and institutions to deliver more comprehensive social protection provision that can respond to any future economic, food or climate shocks in Tanzania</narrative>
  </description>
